   "name": "King T'Challa (Marvel only)",
   "notes": [
    "22 swaps: the 19 nonland cards and 3 lands with no Marvel printing come out.",
    "This is a different deck from the open list. The cards that make every player draw each turn (Howling Mine, Dictate of Kruphix, Vision Skeins, Words of Wisdom, Jace Beleren, Prosperity) have no Marvel printing.",
    "What carries the draw plan instead: Horn of Greed (each player draws when they play a land, which is usually their second card that turn), Wedding Ring, Mind's Eye, Rent Is Due, Super Intelligence and Cut a Deal. Expect one or two T'Challa triggers a round where the open list gets four or more.",
    "It leans harder on the Black Panther side: more fliers (Namor, Black Bolt) and Reconnaissance Mission to draw off combat.",
    "Counterspells drop from seven to four (Counterspell, Arcane Denial, Dismissive Denial, We Say Thee Nay!). Damning Verdict is the copy from the History of Heroes kit; Shang-Chi and Iron Man, Armored Avenger put counters on your own creatures so some survive it.",
    "Black Bolt is the suggested cut from the Fantastic Four deck. If your wife keeps him there, run Captain Marvel's partner slot as Hyperion, Supreme Hero ($5.84) or a second basic.",
    "Prices (Nov 12 snapshot) for the pieces you may not own: Horn of Greed $7.31 (you own one, listed in Doom Unrivaled), Wedding Ring $2.99, Daughter of the Deep $2.07, Captain America, Unbowed $1.79; the rest are under $1.",
    "Not simulated. Weaker than the open list; the other two Marvel-only versions lose much less."
   ],
